"comparison": "Both Goldman Sachs and Morgan Stanley explicitly define their wealth management asset metrics to exclude self-directed client activities, establishing a clear distinction between managed/advisory assets and those where the client retains control. GS defines Assets Under Supervision (AUS) by stating it 'does not include the self-directed brokerage assets of our clients,' while MS defines Daily Average Round Turnover (DARTs) specifically as representing 'total self-directed trades,' thereby isolating activity that MS reports on separately from its discretionary wealth management performance metrics.",
